<title>RUSSIA: Rouble dips as T-bill yields low, trade calm.</title>
<headline>Rouble dips as T-bill yields low, trade calm.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The rouble eased on Monday as bank demand ebbed for funds to invest in government securities, dealers said and added trading was calm at the beginning of the summer season.</p>
<p> roubles/dollar	June 2 midday  June 2 early   May 30 close</p>
<p> today settlement    5,772-73	 5,769-71	 5,769-71</p>
<p> tomorrow settlement 5,776-78	 5,768-70	 5,776-77</p>
<p> overnight credit (%)    1-5		2-7		1-5</p>
<p>			   June 2				May 30</p>
<p> central bank	  5,756/92			    5,756/90</p>
<p> MICEX		   5,768				 5,767</p>
<p>&quot;There was active T-bill buying last week but now it is quiet and it could be due to the beginning of summer (holiday) season,&quot; Neftekhimbank dealer Vladimir Zrazhevsky said.</p>
<p>Dealers said low T-bill yields had made dollar investments more attractive for banks.</p>
<p>--Artyom Danielyan, Moscow newsroom (095) 941 8520</p>
</text>
